  "articleBody": "Grout keeps your tiled surfaces stable and shields backer boards from water, but simple application errors often lead to expensive bathroom repairs. Here are key pitfalls to watch for.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid\n- Adding excessive water during mixing: Thinned grout creates weak, powdery joints that crack easily under foot traffic.\n- Packing grout over dusty joints: Failing to clean out debris prevents proper bonding, leading to early separation.\n- Leaving dried haze on tile faces: Once cementitious grout dries fully on tile surfaces, cleaning becomes difficult and risks scratching tiles.\n- Sealing joints too early: Sealing damp grout traps moisture inside, discoloring lines and destroying sealant adhesion.\n- Applying sealer where not recommended: Certain non-porous tiles or epoxy mixtures reject topical sealers, leaving a sticky, uneven film.\n\nWhat to Do Next\nIf your shower or floor grout is already crumbling, hollow, or discolored, patch jobs usually fail. The crew at HH Remodeling LLC can evaluate your surfaces and restore damaged grout lines cleanly. Call 303-505-0866 to plan your repair.",
